# OPTIONAL hardening. Not needed with the Mosquitto add-on's defaults (no ACL = all allowed).
# With an ACL, every user not listed loses access: also list the add-on's internal users
# `homeassistant` and `addons` and all existing device users (e.g. `topic readwrite #`).
# tk-budget connects as `addons` (credentials from the Supervisor MQTT service).
# Host ids and kid ids share the `timekpr/` namespace: they must never be equal.

# --- one block per client PC (user = tk-agent-<client-host>) -------------------
user tk-agent-<client-host>
# own usage, status (LWT) and events; read too: on start the agent restores its
# counters from its own retained usage if its state file was lost
topic readwrite timekpr/<client-host>/#
# HA discovery for the PC's online sensor
topic write homeassistant/binary_sensor/tk_<client-host>/#
# budget output for all kids
topic read timekpr/+/remaining
topic read timekpr/+/settings

# --- add-ons, incl. tk-budget (Supervisor MQTT service user) --------------------
# Other add-ons share this user, so it keeps full access.
user addons
topic readwrite #

# --- Home Assistant (MQTT integration user) ------------------------------------
# HA core uses this internal user for all MQTT devices, so it keeps full access
# (covers the dashboard writes to timekpr/+/cmd and timekpr/+/set/#).
user homeassistant
topic readwrite #
